[2026-10-16; named HIKP Gaussian-barrier comparison complete]
The HIKP v2 Theorems 4.9/6.1 comparison is complete as a qualified norm, measurement and cost nonmatch. Its best-k-term l2 certificate transfers to C N^-alpha ||x||2 all-bin error only under the additional tail condition (1+epsilon) sigma_k(Ux)_2/||x||2+delta<=C N^-alpha. The flat-spectrum control defeats that certificate for k<N at fixed alpha>1/2 and sufficiently large N. Retain the accepted pathwise Gaussian rank-deficit theorem, arbitrary measurable decoder and transcript-only adaptivity guards. Endpoint alpha=1/2 and other information models remain separate open questions. Parent TO RESEARCH, priority34; no unrestricted runtime, finite-word or novelty claim.
