[2026-10-16; named comparison stop reached]
Only the HIKP source-specific hypothesis/norm/cost mapping is complete. Do not repeat it or replace quantitative pathwise deficit with mere rank deficiency; the accepted random-one-coordinate-omission control remains. A full-input algorithm, nonlinear sparse recovery or an arbitrary adaptive state with raw-input side information is not excluded by the retained theorem. The l2-to-linfinity comparison is a certificate nonmatch, not impossibility of all adaptations. Preserve the unresolved alpha=1/2 endpoint and unchanged alpha<1/2 positive result.
