[2026-10-16; robust unitary frontier gate completed]
Completed: Ailon2014 square-state/every-prefix hypothesis comparison as a qualified nonmatch to the general rectangular/streaming interface, and a robust simultaneous two-register-unitary lemma. If m frontier rows of support exponents h>=n-L have full coefficient-row error eta<1/2, g>=m[(1-eta)(n-L)-h2(eta)]/2. For zero ancillas and original-input row error epsilon<1/8 use eta=sqrt(2epsilon). The exact unitary and fixed-graph results were already accepted. Next constructive gate remains a fully charged sub-N-log-N selected-chirp/frontier algorithm; no such primitive is supplied. Parent TO RESEARCH, priority34.
